{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KQXGQ2e42DZY5X13QyRu7o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, the directory exists. Now let me write the full LaTeX paper. Given the \"worst\" tier and narrative guidance, I need to reframe this as a systematic analysis of measurement error propagation in HTE estimation, with a decision framework for when stratified correction is needed vs when global correction suffices.\n\nKey points for worst tier:\n- \"Debiasing can hurt\" only in extreme (unrealistic) regimes\n- HB has no significant advantage over stratified MLE at n≥200\n- Semi-synthetic shows real LLMs have small Δ error (0.06-0.09)\n\n\n- PPCI outperforms EC-HTE in the moderate regime, though the diagnostic criterion only achieves 0.68 AUROC\n- EC-HTE becomes unreliable when subgroup misspecification exceeds 35% noise, falling below global correction performance\n- The crossover points are quite high, requiring 500-1200 expert labels before stratified approaches justify their complexity\n\nI'll frame the paper as \"When Does Subgroup-Stratified Correction Matter? A Systematic Analysis of Measurement Error Propagation in Heterogeneous Treatment Effect Estimation with LLM Annotations\" — presenting the results honestly and positioning the contribution as a practical decision framework and empirical analysis rather than advocating for a new method.\n\nNow I'm writing the full LaTeX document...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1957,"cache_read_input_tokens":36568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1957},"output_tokens":13,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4317ee69-6295-4009-a36c-b2f5c7193876","uuid":"c3ef65a7-7adc-40e2-b2d1-64dc3b92c137"}
